<speech id="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2013-06-05a.205.0" speakerid="uk.org.publicwhip/member/40130" speakername="Anna Soubry" colnum="205"  time="009:30:00" url="http://www.publications.parliament.uk/pa/cm201314/cmhansrd/cm130605/halltext/130605h0001.htm#130605h0001.htm_spnew9">
	<p pid="a.205.0/1">On the point my hon. Friend made about any rationing of or charging for GP appointments, let me assure her that that was an idea floated on a website and is not Government policy. It is reasonable for people who have an interest in such issues to be able to debate whatever they wish to debate, but it is certainly not Government policy, and I know of no good reason why it ever should be. Furthermore, she makes an important point about the unintended consequences of the number of women training as doctors.</p>
</speech>
